  "slug": "cryo-structure-34d6",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers apply statistical and learned models to noisy cryo-EM and cryo-ET density, with new consistency and label-noise corrections.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is replacing sequential or manually tuned density-processing steps with statistically defined or learned procedures that operate directly on noisy data. Astex-Faro applies a reference-ensemble statistical framework, with a new FSCoh consistency metric, to flag significant density deviations in cryo-EM maps for drug discovery hit identification. RobPicker, a meta-learning framework, corrects label noise and reweights rare species to improve macromolecule particle picking in cryo-ET tomograms. Cadense generates antibody Fv conformational ensembles from sequence, trained to match MD-derived distributions. FlexENN and the cofolding benchmark address binding energy prediction and ligand placement rather than map processing, so the thread is dominant rather than shared by every item. What is new is the explicit handling of noise and reference distributions within learned or statistical density workflows.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
